===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:yelow}}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ǵʰelh₃-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|yelow|yelwe, yelou}}, from {{inh|en|ang|ġeolwe}}, oblique form of {{inh|en|ang|ġeolu}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*gelu}}, from  {{inh|en|gem-pro|*gelwaz}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*ǵʰelh₃wós}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*ǵʰelh₃-||green, yellow}}.

Cognate with {{cog|sco|yella||yellow}}, {{cog|frr|gööl}}, {{m|frr|güül||yellow}}, {{cog|stq|jeel|t=yellow}}, {{cog|fy|giel|t=yellow}}, {{cog|cim|gel}}, {{m|cim|ghéel||yellow}}, {{cog|nl|geel||yellow}}, {{cog|nds-nl|gael}}, {{m|nds-nl|gel||yellow}}, {{cog|de|gelb}}, {{m|de|gehl||yellow}}, {{cog|nds-de|gel}}, {{m|nds-de|geel}}, {{m|nds-de|gęl}}, {{m|nds-de|gäl||yellow}}, {{cog|lb|giel||yellow}}, {{cog|wym|gaoł||yellow}}, {{cog|yi|געל}}, {{m|yi|געלב||yellow}}, {{cog|da,nb,nn,sv|gul||yellow}}, {{cog|fo,is|gulur||yellow}}. Compare also {{cog|cy|gell||bay, tawny}}, {{cog|la|helvus||dull yellow}}, {{cog|ga|geal||white, bright}}, {{cog|lt|žalias||green}}, {{cog|grc|χλωρός||light green}}, {{cog|fa|زرد|tr=zard||yellow}}, {{cog|sa|हरि||greenish-yellow}}, {{cog|ru|жёлтый||yellow}}, {{cog|ru|зелёный||green}}. Not related to {{noncog|it|giallo}}—see {{m|la|galbinus}}.

The verb is from {{inh|en|enm|yelwen}}, {{m|enm|ȝalowen}}, {{m|enm|ȝolewen}}, from {{inh|en|ang|ġeolwian}}, from the adjective.

====Noun====
{{wp}}
{{en-noun|~}}

# The [[color]] of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing [[green]] and [[red]] light, or by subtracting [[blue]] from [[white]] light; the color evoked by light of [[wavelength]] around 580 nm; one of the three [[primary color]]s in [[subtractive]] color systems.
#: {{color panel|fff700}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1892|author=Charlotte Perkins Gilman|title=The Yellow Wallpaper|passage=It is the strangest '''yellow''', that wall-paper! It makes me think of all the yellow things I ever saw—not beautiful ones like buttercups, but old foul, bad yellow things.}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Kristen Rogers|title=Over half of US states are trying to eliminate food dyes. Here’s what you can do now|url=https://www.cnn.com/2025/03/29/health/food-dye-bans-states-wellness|date=2025-03-29|passage=Red No. 3, red No. 40, blue No. 2 and green No. 3 all have been linked with cancer or tumors in animals. Other sources say red No. 40 and '''yellow''' No. 5 and No. 6 contain or may be contaminated with known carcinogens.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261011090009/https://www.cnn.com/2025/03/29/health/food-dye-bans-states-wellness|archivedate=11 October 2026}}
# {{lb|en|US}} The middle light in a set of three [[traffic lights]], the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so.
# {{lb|en|snooker}} One of the [[color]] [[ball]]s used in [[snooker]], with a value of 2 points.
# {{lb|en|pocket billiards}} One of two groups of object balls, or a ball from that group, as used in the principally British version of [[pool#Etymology 2|pool]] that makes use of unnumbered balls (the yellow(s) and red(s)); ''contrast [[stripes]] and [[solids]] in the originally American version with numbered balls'').
# {{lb|en|sports}} A [[yellow card]].
#* {{quote-journal|en| date=April 15, 2011| author=Saj Chowdhury| title=Norwich 2 - 1 Nott'm Forest| work=BBC Sport| url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/13009332.stm| passage=Andrew Surman fired in what proved to be a 37th-minute winner before Forest's Paul Konchesky saw red late on. That second '''yellow''' for the loan signing came in stoppage time and did not affect the outcome of a game which Norwich dominated.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20120201044213/http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/13009332.stm|archivedate=1 February 2012}}
# A yellow dye or pigment.
# A pen, pencil, crayon, etc., made of yellow pigment.
# Something, or a part of a thing, which is yellow.
# Any of various [[pierid]] butterflies of the [[subfamily]] {{taxfmt|Coliadinae|subfamily}}, especially the yellow colored species. Compare [[sulphur]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1869|author={{w|Alfred Russel Wallace}}|title={{w|The Malay Archipelago}}|publisher=Macmillan and Co.|year_published=|volume=I|location=London|page=297|passage=Several other beautiful butterflies rewarded my search in this place [...] The most abundant butterflies were the whites and '''yellows''' (Pieridae), several of which I had already found at Lombock and at Coupang, while others were new to me.}}

